  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bipartite social dialogue for productivity and decent work in Lao PDR led to the signing of a bipartite agreement between the Lao Federation of Trade Unions (LFTU) and Lao National Chambers of Commerce and Industry (LNCCI) to establish the National Bipartite Forum for Social Dialogue &amp; Common Actions &#x2013; the first ever such agreement &#x2013; the agreement aims to promote joint agenda for dialogue with the Government and enterprise level initiatives for workplace cooperation, decent work, and productivity improvements; Constituents set up a six-member bipartite working group to coordinate follow up initiatives for addressing employment, business and labour relations challenges in Lao. ILO, with the support of Japan, provided knowledge and technical support to the social dialogue process of the constituents and assisted in reviewing the priorities and challenges in strengthening social dialogue and labour relations mechanisms in Lao PDR.</narrative>
   </description>
